  "final_answer_preview": "The punishment for hitting someone (assault) depends on the intent and circumstances. If the assault is intended to dishonour the person and is not provoked, the punishment can be imprisonment for a term that may extend to two years, or a fine, or both (Section 133, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023). If the assault occurs without grave provocation, the punishment may be imprisonment for up to three months or a fine of up to one thousand rupees (Section 131, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023).",
